      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2014 Japan Society for Endoscopic Surgery, Asia Endosurgery Task Force and Wiley Publishing Asia Pty Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "Laparoscopic sleeve gastrectomy (LSG) is the most common bariatric procedure performed in Asia. Staple-line leaks post LSG are notoriously difficult to treat. Here we report a case of a gastro-colic fistula after a post-LSG leak. While reperforming laparoscopy and/or stenting remain the mainstay of early leak management, chronic complications such as a gastro-colic fistula are rare and require a tailor-made approach. Stenting alone has a limited role in managing chronic fistulas after LSG."
      },
